            "subtitle": "Average increase",
            "percentage": 49,
            "value_label": "+49%",
            "caption": "average rise in SHBG \u2014 the protein that mops up excess hormones \u2014 after 6 months*\u2021",
            "button_label": "What is SHBG",
            "popup_heading": "SHBG",
            "popup_stat": "+49%",
            "popup_stat_text": "average rise in SHBG after 6 months on 40:1 inositol \u2014 with no real change in the placebo group*\u2021",
            "popup_info_text": "SHBG is a protein that binds spare hormones \u2014 including testosterone \u2014 so they can't act on the body. More SHBG means less active testosterone in circulation. Estradiol, a key cycle hormone, also more than doubled in the same group."
