          "type": "info_button",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Why progesterone",
            "popup_title": "Progesterone \u2014 the Ovulation Marker",
            "popup_text": "<p>Progesterone only rises after an egg has been released \u2014 so a blood test for it is how researchers prove ovulation actually happened, no guesswork. In the 40:1 group it was rising significantly by the end of month one.</p>"
          }
        },
        "info_2": {
          "type": "info_button",
          "settings": {
            "label": "What is SHBG",
            "popup_title": "SHBG",
            "popup_text": "<p>SHBG is a protein that binds spare hormones \u2014 including testosterone \u2014 so they can't act on the body. More SHBG means less active testosterone in circulation. In this trial, SHBG and estradiol both rose most with the 40:1 blend.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
